# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/ is generated, never committed. Everything under it is ignored and the
# few small committed sets are re-allowed explicitly. A whitelist (rather than
# one ignore rule per new directory) is what stops the next multi-GB rollout
# dump from riding along in a `git add -A`. data/README.md says how to
# regenerate each of them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/data/**
!/data/README.md
!/data/demo/
!/data/demo/**

# Model weights and training dumps, wherever they land
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.h5
checkpoints/
wandb/
mlruns/
runs/

# Telemetry stores and blob dirs, at any depth
**/obs.db
**/obs.db-*
**/obs_blobs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and raw tensors are ignored by default, but docs/ holds the proof the
# results documents cite — training curves, pod logs, the calibration bundle —
# and data/demo/ holds the bundled rollouts. Both are re-allowed here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.npy
*.npz
*.safetensors
!docs/**/*.log
!docs/**/*.npz
!docs/**/*.safetensors
# ...except the 66 MB GRPO LoRA. It is the artifact of a negative result and it lives on the HF
# Hub; adapter_config.json next to it records the run configuration, which is the part worth reading.
docs/**/grpo_adapter/*.safetensors
!/data/demo/**

# macos / editors
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
